A||||10||Dan87GT||Removing the Air Conditioning||||10
Z||000000||Dan87GT||09-28-1999||09:26 AM||||I have removed the engine and transmission from my 87 GT and would like to disconnect the air conditioning compressor but am afraid of what might happen, is there a procedure to depressurize the system so I can remove the compressor? The car needs a new compressor anyhow.||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||09-28-1999||09:35 AM||||It is a felony in the US to release Freon into the atmosphere. The system needs to be pumped down by a trained & licenses tech. Opening the system without pumping it down can hurt you. If the escaping freon hits you you can freeze skin and fingers real quick.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan87GT||09-28-1999||10:34 AM||||I forgot to mention that I live in Mexico, really far south of the border||||reg||1
Z||000003||chris6878||09-28-1999||11:30 AM||||Im removed the engine in my 85 GT and i didnt have to disconnect my a/c...  i just unbolted it from the motor and let it hang there until the engine was put back in.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   CHRIS||||reg||4
Z||000004||Dan87GT||09-28-1999||03:05 PM||||The compressor is shot so I have to replace it, it hasen't worked in years. Also I want to replace the lines since I heard that they will probably leak anyhow. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-28-1999||08:58 PM||||you still need to evacuate the system.<P>you can have new soft line put on the old hardware as long as it's good.||||reg||1
Z||000006||RICK||09-28-1999||09:07 PM||||Dan, try going to a tech-college in you area that has a HVAC class.  They would probbly do it for free since it would be a class project.  You might even get them to pressure test your system (placing high pressure nitrogen in the lines to test for leaks).||||reg||6
Z||000007||Carrolles||09-29-1999||12:29 PM||||The chances are that if the compressor has been shot for years there is no pressure in the system anyway.  You can put a gage on the low pressure port at the dryer to verify this.  You can purchase a cheap gage that looks like a tire pressure gage  for about $5 at most auto parts stores.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dan87GT||09-29-1999||01:41 PM||||So how do I depressurize the system??||||reg||1
Z||000009||Carrolles||09-29-1999||06:09 PM||||If your pressure is gone then you can simply disconnect the fitting at the compressor. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||batboy||09-29-1999||09:12 PM||||If the A/C system is still pressurized, you must take it to a certified shop that will evacuate the system. To vent freon into the atmosphere is not only illegal, but not very smart. Maybe you like getting skin cancer and other ailments due to destroying the ozone, but I don't.||||reg||1
